                  "language": "en",
                  "format": "text/html",
                  "value": "<p><b>One enslaved boy's journey</b></p> <p>'While 'the Bedford' was in Kingston, the enslaved people trafficked onboard began to be sold to enslavers and plantations on the island. This included one enslaved male who was trafficked to Port Royal by Robert Ambrose. In 1817, Ambrose registered six enslaved individuals as his 'property'. This included two young men born in Africa, George and Edward, who were both said to be twenty four years old. One of these men was almost certainly trafficked from the Congo River by 'the Bedford' when they were around just twelve years old.</p>"
                }
              ],
